    "text": "Here's the implementation of the `decimal_to_binary` function:\n\n```pythondef decimal_to_binary(decimal):\n\n    if decimal is None: return  \"\"\n    \n    binary = \"\"\n    while decimal > 0:\n        binary = str(decimal % 2) + binary\n        decimal = decimal // 2\n    \n    return \"db\" + binary + \"db\"\n```\n\nThis function converts the decimal number to its binary representation as a string, and then wraps it with \"db\" at the beginning",
